raceLogger interface{}\n\ntype TracingEvent struct{}\n\nfunc traceInitState(*raft) {}\n\nfunc traceReady(*raft) {}\n\nfunc traceCommit(*raft) {}\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/usr/bin/python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nrun='30c25f44a82b4d0c81c3b3b6e2d9d883';art='76ae6ec5c0e049cb8d703d9140f48040'\nids=['S-joint-contract','S-joint-flag','S-applied','S-abort','S-heartbeat-tick','S-formation','S-changer','S-advance','S-raw-advance','S-raw-transfer','S-raft-state','S-log-state','S-unstable-state','S-storage-state','S-config-clone','S-status-clone','S-random-timeout','S-trace-disabled']\nrationale='Applicability: the accepted v1 claim and bindings assign implicit joint departure to Raft when possible (S-joint-contract and S-joint-flag). The fixed input explicitly chooses JointImplicit; it does not reinterpret explicit joint mode or impose a ten-tick completion deadline. The entering change is applied before Advance, so the separate paused early-Advance dispute does not apply. History: the fixed harness creates the declared three-voter initial snapshot, elects node 1 using implementation-generated messages, persists each Ready before sends, and commits removal of node 3 at index 3 in term 2. It applies that configuration, requests transfer to voter 2 before completing the same Ready, then completes Advance. This is serialized public RawNode activity with no forged acknowledgements. One generated TimeoutNow is dropped during the transfer attempt; every message and every Ready is processed in the later suffix. Actual admission records applied=3, transfer_clear=true and the original leader, with no omitted application callback.\\\\n\\\\nObservation/correlation: fixed corrected lines 121-122 read active raft.trk.Config.AutoLeave and outgoing voters under exclusive single-thread ownership; Status only supplies its unaffected scalar fields and a separate status_auto_leave diagnostic. The active_result event is correlated to admitted by scenario, leader=1 and joint_index=3, independent of compared state values. Current run '+run+' exited 0, reported cycle_equal=true, active auto_leave=true, joint=true, transfer_clear=true, no leave proposals in the cycle or total, and applied=commit=3. I reconstructed split Go JSON output chunks and independently compared the two retained 8915-character state strings: they are identical. The encoded closed_joint_cycle=true therefore violates the assertion that this admitted operation must not reach that cycle. The previous artifact sampled the lossy Status copy; this correction answers the exact observation issue without changing inputs or weakening the requirement.\\\\n\\\\nRecurrence and endpoint: recursive capture covers all three RawNodes, raft state, term/vote/roles, fixed configuration, peer progress/inflight arrays, timers, pending reads/messages, complete log/storage values, unstable state and saved Ready completion steps. The scheduler drains its local queue and requires HasReady=false at each capture. It repeats the same ordered Tick-all/drain schedule for a full ten-tick period and checks roles and term after ticks and protocol mutations. No goroutines, external callbacks or pending client work exist. Logger output, unused trace logger, single-thread MemoryStorage mutex and monotonic call instrumentation are excluded; S-storage-state shows counters only increment and are never used for a storage decision. Slice capacity/pointer identity do not affect this no-append heartbeat cycle. Function entry identities plus the recursively captured receiver state determine callbacks here. The global RNG is not sampled in this suffix: resetRandomizedElectionTimeout is reached through role/term reset, while the fixed unchanged roles and frequent heartbeat delivery keep followers below election timeout. Thus this is a repeatable closed protocol suffix, not an inference of infinite stalling from a finite wait. The source corroborates the missing trigger: only appliedTo attempts leave; transfer abort clears a field, and an idle heartbeat suffix produces no further application completion.\\\\n\\\\nCompletion/counterevidence: a separately tagged client rescue after the principal result generates one leave proposal and finishes at applied=commit=5 with joint=false. This shows a later stimulus can rescue the transition, but the caller is not required to issue it for an implicit transition. All generated work drains before normal successful return. The observation supports the scoped lost automatic continuation, not failure under every schedule or consensus safety loss.'\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id=art,rationale='Review the corrected fixed execution and resolve the inherited copy-observation issue against its answering artifact.',sources=[dict(id='S-random-timeout',file='raft.go',start_line=2042,end_line=2051,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='S-trace-disabled',file='state_trace_nop.go',start_line=15,end_line=35,kind='code_observation')],review_items=[dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=ids,rationale=rationale,counterevidence=[],limitations=['No consensus-safety violation or production latency bound was checked.','A new proposal, manual leave, or leadership change may rescue departure; they change the steady input policy.','The earlier version retains its measured holds result and invalid observation; only the corrected version receives this correspondence.','The separate Status/Clone fidelity discrepancy has not yet received its own fixed obligation/check.'],report_title='领导权转移超时后，隐式联合配置缺少自动退出触发',report_answer='修正观测后，节点在转移超时、应用完成且正常处理心跳的情况下，完整协议状态每十个 tick 重复，AutoLeave 仍为真且没有退出提案。额外客户端提案随后触发退出；该结果指向自动续行缺失，不是共识安全违例。')],resolutions=[dict(issue_id='e1eeee7602dc462387caaba045e935ae',source_ids=['S-config-clone','S-status-clone','S-joint-flag','S-raft-state'],evidence_ids=[art,run],rationale='The new fixed active_result reads the live flag and retains the copied false flag separately. Fresh execution observes live true/status false and a violated closed-cycle comparison. This answers the lossy-copy observation/oracle issue on v2 while leaving v1 unchanged; the admitted history, requirement, and logical forbidden condition are preserved.',residual_issue_ids=[],scope_limitations=['Resolution applies to corrected v2 and descendants, not to the old artifact.','No independent formal finding about Config.Clone is attributed here.'])],feedback=dict(ref_ids=[run,'741e5e2156e4421abc1c95cb51fe0704','F-auto-joint','B-application','B-context','S-config-clone','S-status-clone'],answered='Corrected run '+run+' completed with a violated closed-cycle comparison: active AutoLeave=true, copied Status flag=false, exact repeated protocol state, no leave proposals, and completed joint entry at index 3. A later independent client proposal triggered one leave and application through index 5. The current review explains recurrence and resolves the inherited observation issue against the new artifact.',remaining=['Retain the lost application-trigger continuation as the answered proposition in the next related map handoff.','Investigate the separately sourced configuration-copy fidelity responsibility without reusing this claim.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The current observation directly measures the active flag consumed by appliedTo; retained raw state and source establish the scoped recurrence argument.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission-autoleave-confirm.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_08-49-50-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission-autoleave-confirm.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
